PulseNest host unit tests (Unity)
=================================

One directory per suite: test_lib/test_<name>/test_<name>.cpp. Each suite is a plain Unity program
(setUp/tearDown/main with UNITY_BEGIN/RUN_TEST/UNITY_END) that includes only incunest_afe4490.h,
unity.h and the C standard library, so it builds and runs on the host PC.

The library is compiled for the host with -DUNIT_TEST (opens the test_* accessors) together with
incunest_afe4490_hal_host.cpp (no-op GPIO/SPI, fake FreeRTOS/esp_log/esp_timer).

Build and run everything (needs cmake, ninja and a host g++ on PATH — MinGW-w64 on Windows):

    python test_lib/runner/run_host_tests.py
    python test_lib/runner/run_host_tests.py hr1 spo2    # only suites matching a filter
    python test_lib/runner/run_host_tests.py --clean     # rebuild from scratch

Build system: test_lib/runner/CMakeLists.txt (Unity 2.6.0 vendored in test_lib/runner/unity).
